    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Ten Year War is a lavish Black Sabbath box set that celebrates the band’s first eight Ozzy Osbourne-era studio albums, presenting them as a unified statement of early heavy metal. Released through BMG, it gathers Black Sabbath, Paranoid, Master of Reality, Vol. 4, Sabbath Bloody Sabbath, Sabotage, Technical Ecstasy, and Never Say Die! in remastered form, emphasizing the group’s evolution from doom-laden blues-rock into darker, more elaborate and experimental territory.\n\nBeyond the albums themselves, the set’s significance lies in its presentation of Sabbath’s legacy: rare 7-inch singles, a hardcover book, reproduced memorabilia, and a crucifix-shaped USB loaded with the albums in high-resolution audio. The package was issued as a limited-edition collector’s item, and its focus on original tapes, archival material, and deluxe artwork helped frame Black Sabbath not just as metal pioneers, but as a band whose 1970s run remained culturally and sonically definitive.",
